<BaseLayout title="Accessories" description="A/C, gas pedals, clutch master, and accessory drive notes for LS Gen Coupe swaps.">
  <h1>Accessories</h1>
  <p>
    Accessory drive spacing, A/C retention, pedal choice, and clutch hydraulics all affect how "daily-able" the finished car feels.
  </p>

  <h2>A/C System</h2>
  <p>
    Wire colors for A/C request vary by year. Verify with power on and the A/C button pressed.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>2010 2.0T example:</strong> Yellow and Blue wires on the A/C control module.</li>
    <li><strong>2013 3.8:</strong> Same colors on the larger plug leading to the passenger-side fuse box.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Gas Pedal</h2>
  <p>
    Cable or drive-by-wire options exist. Several builders have documented keeping the OEM pedal or using a GM pedal with Holley.
  </p>

